   "questiontext_html": "<p>Write a Python program that reads three whole numbers (one per line) and prints their average.</p>\n<p><b>Note:</b> the average may be a decimal number. To avoid tiny floating-point mismatches, print your answer rounded to 2 decimal places using <code>round(value, 2)</code>. For example, <code>print(round(3.33333, 2))</code> prints <code>3.33</code>.</p>\n<p><b>Example:</b> Input: <pre>3\n6\n9</pre> Output: <pre>6.0</pre></p>",
