   "xml_name": "PS2_033_Function Is Perfect Number",
   "display_name": "Is Perfect Number",
   "questiontext_html": "<p>A <b>perfect number</b> is a whole number that is exactly equal to the sum of its <b>proper divisors</b> - all the whole numbers smaller than it that divide it evenly (not counting the number itself). For example, 6 is perfect because its proper divisors 1, 2, 3 add up to 6. And 28 is perfect (1+2+4+7+14 = 28). But 10 is not (1+2+5 = 8).</p>\n<p>Write a function named <code>is_perfect</code> that takes a whole number <code>n</code> and <b>returns</b> <code>True</code> if it is a perfect number, or <code>False</code> otherwise.</p>\n<p>You may assume <code>n</code> is always greater than 1.</p>\n<p><b>Example:</b> <code>is_perfect(6)</code> should return <code>True</code>. <code>is_perfect(10)</code> should return <code>False</code>.</p>",
