   "xml_name": "PS2_036_Function Recursive GCD",
   "display_name": "Recursive GCD",
   "questiontext_html": "<p>The <b>Greatest Common Divisor (GCD)</b> of two positive integers is the largest whole number that divides both of them exactly. Euclid's method computes it like this: the GCD of <code>a</code> and <code>b</code> equals the GCD of <code>b</code> and <code>a % b</code>, and when the second number becomes 0, the first number is the answer.</p>\n<p>Write a <b>recursive</b> function named <code>gcd</code> that takes two positive integers (int &gt; 0) <code>a</code> and <code>b</code> and <b>returns</b> their GCD. Your function must be recursive (it must call itself), with a correct base case.</p>\n<p><b>Example:</b> <code>gcd(12, 18)</code> should return <code>6</code>.</p>",
